---
import SubLayout from '../layouts/SubLayout.astro';
---

<SubLayout title="HARDWARE MANIFEST" section="HARDWARE MANIFEST"
  classification="CLASSIFICATION: BUILD REFERENCE / STATUS: ACTIVE"
  introLines={[
    "This is a parts list.",
    "It is also a set of instructions.",
    "The distinction is intentional.",
  ]}
  introAction="[ VIEW MANIFEST ]">

  <h2>CORE COMPONENTS</h2>
  <table class="data-table">
    <thead><tr><th>COMPONENT</th><th>SPEC</th><th>ROLE</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Flipper Zero</td><td>STM32WB55 / 128×64 LCD</td><td>Operator interface</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Heltec WiFi LoRa 32 V3</td><td>ESP32-S3 / SX1262 / 915MHz</td><td>Mesh radio node, sensor hub</td></tr>
      <tr><td>PINGEQUA ProtoBoard</td><td>Flipper GPIO breakout</td><td>Clean sensor mounting</td></tr>
      <tr><td>LiPo battery</td><td>JST-PH, 3.7V</td><td>Heltec power — independent</td></tr>
      <tr><td>915MHz antenna</td><td>SMA or IPEX</td><td>Required before powering radio</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>SENSOR EXPANSION (PLANNED)</h2>
  <table class="data-table">
    <thead><tr><th>SENSOR</th><th>INTERFACE</th><th>FUNCTION</th><th>PHASE</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>BME280</td><td>I2C (0x76)</td><td>Temp / humidity / pressure</td><td>07</td></tr>
      <tr><td>MAX17048</td><td>I2C (0x36)</td><td>LiPo fuel gauge</td><td>09</td></tr>
      <tr><td>BN-220 GPS</td><td>UART1 9600 baud</td><td>Position + timestamp</td><td>08</td></tr>
      <tr><td>HC-SR04</td><td>GPIO 21/47</td><td>Proximity — dead-drop detection</td><td>11</td></tr>
      <tr><td>SW-520D tilt</td><td>GPIO 2</td><td>Tamper — node disturbed</td><td>10</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Slide switch</td><td>GPIO 4 / Flipper pin 15</td><td>Physical arm/disarm</td><td>10</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Photoresistor</td><td>ADC GPIO 5</td><td>Tamper — case opened</td><td>10</td></tr>
      <tr><td>IR receiver</td><td>GPIO 48</td><td>Remote arm/disarm ~10m</td><td>10</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Vibration motor</td><td>Flipper pin 6 via AO3400</td><td>Haptic RX alert</td><td>10</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Active buzzer</td><td>Flipper pin 5 via PN2222</td><td>Audible RX alert</td><td>10</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>BASE WIRING — 3 WIRES</h2>
  <div class="code-block"><pre>Flipper U_TX (pin 13)  →  Heltec GPIO7  (Serial module RX)
Flipper U_RX (pin 14)  →  Heltec GPIO6  (Serial module TX)
Flipper GND            →  Heltec GND

DO NOT connect power rails.
Each device runs from its own battery.</pre></div>
  <p>Runs the Meshtastic Serial module in PROTO mode (RX 7, TX 6, 115200,
  override-console off). Not GPIO43/44 — the CP2102 USB bridge clamps those on
  battery, so the old link died the moment you unplugged the cable.</p>

  <h2>POWER ARCHITECTURE</h2>
  <p>No shared power between devices. The Flipper's 3.3V regulator cannot source
  the 200–500mA the ESP32-S3 draws under load.</p>
  <div class="code-block"><pre>[Flipper battery]  →  Flipper Zero       (independent)
[Heltec battery]   →  Heltec ESP32-S3    (independent)
                            │
                       [GPIO26 Vext]  →  Sensor 3.3V rail</pre></div>

  <h2>SAFETY NOTES</h2>
  <p><span class="tag tag--warn">REQUIRED</span> Attach the 915MHz antenna before
  powering the Heltec. Running the SX1262 without an antenna risks RF damage.</p>
  <p><span class="tag tag--warn">REQUIRED</span> Install the 1N4007 flyback diode
  across the vibration motor terminals before the MOSFET. The motor is an inductive
  load — without the diode, back-EMF spikes will damage the AO3400.</p>
  <p><span class="tag tag--warn">NOTE</span> Standard HC-SR04 requires 5V. Verify
  your module's datasheet. The Heltec 5V pin is only live when USB-powered.</p>

  <div class="scene-divider">
    <p>Full pinout and sensor wiring →
      <a href="https://github.com/ComplacencyKillz/GhostMesh/blob/main/docs/wiring.md"
         target="_blank" rel="noopener">docs/wiring.md</a>
    </p>
  </div>

</SubLayout>
